{
  "source": {
    "coordinate_system": "slot_image",
    "artifact": "the 2.158.15 capsule's slot image",
    "sha256": "00393be197569851c9a72bd214cf22f45a04b7e1fc759ab4ccc68c98dd650d78",
    "coordinate_space": "slot image; the metadata block is the 0xd0-byte sub-image header at the offset the descriptor chain gives"
  },
  "what_this_is": "the per-component metadata block that precedes each encrypted payload, read as fields at their offsets. Nothing here is decrypted",
  "observed_structure": {
    "header": "version 1, length 0xd0, then a 16-byte label at +0x10 (e.g. 'BL31', 'SPBM_FMC-1.0.0')",
    "at_0x40": "12 bytes, unique per component",
    "at_0x50": "the ASCII tag 'AAD' plus padding",
    "at_0x60": "16 bytes, unique per component",
    "at_0x90": "the ASCII tag 'AAD' again",
    "at_0xb0": "32 bytes, unique per component"
  },
  "reading": "a 12-byte nonce and a 16-byte tag beside an 'AAD' label is the shape of an AEAD construction (AES-GCM uses a 12-byte IV and a 16-byte tag). [INFERENCE] on the cipher: the artifacts name no algorithm and no key id.",
  "cipher_claim": {
    "status": "inferred",
    "algorithm": null
  },
  "why_this_closes_the_offline_route": [
    "all 15 metadata blocks carry distinct nonces, so there is no keystream or counter reuse to exploit",
    "the payloads are authenticated, so a modified or truncated image is detectable \u2014 no oracle",
    "no standard compressor header is present at the body (zlib, lzma, xz, zstd, lz4 all refuse), so it is not merely compressed",
    "one capsule boots on every unit, so the key is SoC-family, not per-device, and lives where no artifact reaches: mask ROM or fuses"
  ],
  "what_is_not_claimed": "that the cipher is AES-GCM, that a key exists in any artifact, or that the payloads are undecryptable in principle. They are undecryptable from these bytes without the key, which is a different statement.",
